title: '[revive] pgas as storage deposit'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: "## Storage deposits backed by PGAS\n\nThis PR adds a second payment\
    \ backend for pallet-revive storage deposits: instead of always charging the user\
    \ in native currency (DOT), a runtime can opt in to having deposits denominated\
    \ in **PGAS**\n\n### New trait: `Deposit`\n\n`substrate/frame/revive/src/deposit_payment.rs`\n\
    \nA new sealed `Deposit<T: Config>` trait abstracts over how storage deposits\
    \ are charged, held, refunded, and collected. It has two implementations in-crate:\n\
    \n- **`()`**: the default, charges and refunds the native currency. Identical\
    \ to the existing pre-PR behavior.\n- **`PGasDeposit<Mutator, Holder, Id, RefundPercent>`**:\
    \ the PGAS-backed backend\n\nThe trait is wired into `Config::Deposit` and called\
    \ from `charge_deposit` / `refund_deposit` in place of the direct `T::Currency`\
    \ calls that used to live there.\n\n### New storage: `NativeDepositOf`\n\n`substrate/frame/revive/src/lib.rs`\n\
    \n```rust\npub(crate) type NativeDepositOf<T: Config> = StorageDoubleMap<\n  \
    \  _, Identity, T::AccountId,\n    Blake2_128Concat, T::AccountId,\n    BalanceOf<T>,\
    \ ValueQuery,\n>;\n```\n\nKeyed `(holder_account, user) -> native_amount`. It\
    \ records how much **native currency** a user has contributed to a given account's\
    \ hold. The holder is either a contract (for storage deposits on contract accounts)\
    \ or the pallet account (for code-upload deposits).\n\nIt exists because in the\
    \ mixed PGAS/DOT world, a user's refund cap needs to be tracked explicitly: we\
    \ can't just look at what's on hold because PGAS and DOT are both on hold under\
    \ the same reason. The map caps how much of a refund can come back as DOT ; anything\
    \ beyond that is settled in PGAS.\n\n### `PGasDeposit<Mutator, Holder, Id, RefundPercent>`\n\
    \n`substrate/frame/revive/src/deposit_payment.rs`\n\nParameterized by four type\
    \ parameters that the runtime wires up:\n\n- `Mutator: fungibles::Mutate` \u2014\
    \ the fungibles impl backing PGAS (e.g. `pallet-assets`).\n- `Holder: fungibles::MutateHold`\
    \ \u2014 the holds backend (e.g. `pallet-assets-holder`).\n- `Id: Get<AssetId>`\
    \ \u2014 the PGAS asset id on that fungibles instance.\n- `RefundPercent: Get<Perbill>`\
    \ \u2014 the fraction of PGAS returned on refund/collect; the rest is burned.\n\
    \nCharge semantics:\n- If the user has enough reducible PGAS, the full amount\
    \ is paid in PGAS and no DOT is touched.\n- Otherwise the charge falls through\
    \ to DOT, and the contribution is recorded in `NativeDepositOf` so it can be refunded\
    \ as DOT later.\n\nRefund / collect semantics:\n- DOT is returned first, capped\
    \ by `NativeDepositOf[holder][user]` (and by `Precision::BestEffort` on the actual\
    \ DOT hold).\n- Any shortfall is taken from the PGAS hold. `RefundPercent` of\
    \ that PGAS is transferred to the user's free balance; the remainder is burned.\n\
    \nThe `RefundPercent` burn is what prevents free-PGAS harvesting: a user can't\
    \ deposit storage, release it, and walk away with an allowance they can spend\
    \ on execution.\n\n### Migration (v4)\n\n`substrate/frame/revive/src/migrations/v4.rs`\n\
    \nExisting chains have storage deposits already held in DOT. The migration moves\
    \ existing deposits over to the new accounting in two phases:\n\n**Phase 1** iterates\
    \ `CodeInfoOf` and for each uploaded code credits the uploader's existing `CodeUploadDepositReserve`\
    \ DOT hold into `NativeDepositOf[pallet_account][owner]`.  This is needed so code-upload\
    \ deposits can still be refunded in DOT once the PGAS path is live.\n\n**Phase\
    \ 2** iterates `AccountInfoOf` and for each contract calls `Deposit::migrate_native_to_pgas`,\
    \ which:\n1. Burns the native `StorageDepositReserve` hold from the contract.\n\
    2. Mints the same amount of PGAS into the contract.\n3. Places the minted PGAS\
    \ on hold under the same reason.\n\nPre-PR DOT deposits weren't tracked per-contributor,\
    \ so leaving them as DOT would let users harvest free DOT by refunding against\
    \ deposits they never paid."
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-pgas-allowance
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
